      "identityStatus": "needs_confirmation",
      "categoryID": 2,
      "benefits": "Demonstrated human trial benefit: coadministered subcutaneous cagrilintide and semaglutide produced greater weight reduction than placebo in adults with overweight or obesity without diabetes receiving lifestyle intervention. In the 68-week REDEFINE 1 randomized phase 3 trial, more participants achieved substantial weight-loss thresholds. These findings apply to the studied combination and population, not arbitrary mixtures or untested routes."
    }
